","name":"Moulton, Lawrence H","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pingping","key":"zhangpingpingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Pingping","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elizabeth","key":"begierelizabethpau","last":"Begier","name":"Begier, Elizabeth","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tor","key":"bieringsørensentorpau","last":"Biering-Sørensen","name":"Biering-Sørensen, Tor","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40888695"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmoa2509810","issn":["00284793","15334406"],"issn_org":["00284793"],"journal":"The New England Journal of Medicine","publisher":"Massachussetts Medical Society","status":"e","title":"The New England Journal of Medicine"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["aau-d3fe68d5-69e1-408a-a899-4f43841e1569"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"RSV Prefusion F Vaccine for Prevention of Hospitalization in Older Adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-824020","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Influenza vaccination reduces the risk of adverse outcomes in patients with cardiovascular disease (CVD). We sought to evaluate whether the presence of CVD modified the relative effectiveness of the high-dose quadrivalent influenza vaccine (QIV-HD) versus standard-dose quadrivalent influenza vaccine (QIV-SD) in this prespecified analysis of the DANFLU-1 trial (Feasibility of Randomizing Danish Citizens Aged 65-79 Years to High-Dose Quadrivalent Influenza Vaccine Versus Standard-Dose Quadrivalent Influenza Vaccine in a Pragmatic Registry-Based Setting). METHODS: DANFLU-1 was a pragmatic, open-label, randomized feasibility trial of QIV-HD versus QIV-SD in adults aged 65 to 79 years during the 2021/2022 influenza season in Denmark. Vaccines were allocated in a 1:1 ratio. Baseline and follow-up data regarding diagnoses and mortality were obtained from Danish national registers. The trial is registered at Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT05048589. The CVDs assessed included heart failure, ischemic heart disease, atrial fibrillation, and a combined group denoted chronic CVD consisting of the aforementioned diseases, among others. Prespecified outcomes included hospitalizations for pneumonia or influenza, respiratory disease, CVD, cardiorespiratory disease, all-cause hospitalizations, and mortality. Effect modification was tested using interaction terms. RESULTS: The final study population included 12 477 participants (mean age of 71.7±3.9 years and 5877 [47.1%] were female), of whom 2540 (20.4%) had chronic CVD. QIV-HD versus QIV-SD was associated with a lower incidence of hospitalizations for pneumonia or influenza (incidence rate ratio [IRR], 0.30 [95% CI, 0.14-0.64]) and all-cause mortality (IRR, 0.51 [95% CI, 0.30-0.86]) regardless of chronic CVD (Pinteraction=0.57 and 0.49, respectively). The relative effectiveness of QIV-HD versus QIV-SD against all-cause hospitalizations was modified in participants with chronic CVD (overall: IRR, 0.87 [95% CI, 0.76-0.99]; no chronic CVD: IRR, 0.79 [95% CI, 0.67-0.92]; chronic CVD: IRR, 1.11 [95% CI, 0.88-1.39]; Pinteraction=0.026). No other effect modification was observed by the presence of chronic CVD, heart failure, ischemic heart disease, or atrial fibrillation. CONCLUSIONS: The relative effectiveness of QIV-HD versus QIV-SD was consistent against hospitalizations for pneumonia or influenza and all-cause mortality regardless of chronic CVD. However, the relative effectiveness against all-cause hospitalizations was modified by the presence of chronic CVD. These results should be considered hypothesis generating. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT05048589.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Christensen, Jacob","Johansen, Niklas Dyrby","Modin, Daniel","Janstrup, Kira Hyldekær","Nealon, Joshua","Samson, Sandrine","Loiacono, Matthew","Harris, Rebecca","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Jensen, Anne Marie Reimer","Landler, Nino Emanuel","Claggett, Brian L.","Solomon, Scott D.","Gislason, Gunnar H.","Køber, Lars","Landray, Martin J.","Sivapalan, Pradeesh","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Biering-Sørensen, Tor"],"cuid":["S02-089.10-804122"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Biering-Sørensen, Tor"],"country":["France","Singapore","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brigham and Women’s Hospital","Harvard University","Sanofi","Sanofi Singapore","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Feasibility Studies","Humans","Influenza Vaccines","Pneumonia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relative effectiveness of high dose versus standard dose quadrivalent influenza vaccine in older adults with cardiovascular disease a prespecified analysis of the danflu 000000000001 randomized clinical trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85215266734","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.10-804122","identifier":[{"id":"85215266734","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39215646","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-82871f92-6beb-4db3-85ad-578f09fc5741","ku-d794e858-4847-4613-b076-37649898428b"],"keyword":["atrial fibrillation","feasibility studies","humans","influenza vaccines","pneumonia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-357B43E1DC30336ED541610E000A7A3A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"sanofi","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sanofi","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"sg","key":"sanofi singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Sanofi Singapore","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"harvard university","