k","first":"Jacob","key":"steinmetzpau","last":"Steinmetz","locid":"fc3ac4ad-1c4d-492e-bc3c-330a8af4e5be","name":"Steinmetz, Jacob","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Helle Collatz","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b05bae82-5e32-4f10-980c-147b4af03d6a","name":"Christensen, Helle Collatz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40009541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mej.0000000000001203","issn":["09699546","14735695"],"issn_org":["09699546"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Emergency Medicine","pages":"150","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Emergency Medicine","title_org":"European journal of emergency medicine : official journal of the European Society for Emergency Medicine","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000000409"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk","danish air ambulance"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ef07df41-bbad-4641-aa30-a46dfe96884e","ku-8c45e93e-054f-4c8d-96e1-8baf17b081d7","sdu-ad7ff6de-cc53-4a30-a197-a19e0a370aeb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"In response to comment on : Prehospital interventions and outcomes in traumatic cardiac arrest: a population-based cohort study using Danish helicopter emergency medical services data","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.52-804282","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The population-based Inter99 cohort has contributed extensively to our understanding of effects of a systematic screening and lifestyle intervention, as well as the multifactorial aetiology of type 2 diabetes (T2D) and cardiovascular disease. To understand causes, trajectories and patterns of early and overt cardiometabolic disease manifestations, we will perform a combined clinical deep phenotyping and registry follow-up study of the now 50-80 years old Inter99 participants. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: The Inter99 cohort comprises individuals aged 30-60 years, who lived in a representative geographical area of greater Copenhagen, Denmark, in 1999. Age-stratified and sex-stratified random subgroups were invited to participate in either a lifestyle intervention (N=13 016) or questionnaires (N=5264), while the rest served as a reference population (N=43 021). Of the 13 016 individuals assigned to the lifestyle intervention group, 6784 (52%) accepted participation in a baseline health examination in 1999, including screening for cardiovascular risk factors and prediabetic conditions. In total, 6004 eligible participants, who participated in the baseline examination, will be invited to participate in the deep phenotyping 20-year follow-up clinical examination including measurements of anthropometry, blood pressure, arterial stiffness, cardiometabolic biomarkers, coronary artery calcification, heart rate variability, heart rhythm, liver stiffness, fundus characteristics, muscle strength and mass, as well as health and lifestyle questionnaires. In a subsample, 10-day monitoring of diet, physical activity and continuous glucose measurements will be performed. Fasting blood, urine and faecal samples to be stored in a biobank. The established database will form the basis of multiple analyses. A main purpose is to investigate whether low birth weight independent of genetics, lifestyle and glucose tolerance predicts later common T2D cardiometabolic comorbidities. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study was approved by the Medical Ethics Committee, Capital Region, Denmark (H-20076231) and by the Danish Data Protection Agency through the Capital Region of Denmark's registration system (P-2020-1074). Informed consent will be obtained before examinations. Findings will be disseminated in peer-reviewed journals, at conferences and via presentations to stakeholders, including patients and public health policymakers. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05166447.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Bjørnsbo, Kirsten Schroll","Brøns, Charlotte","Aadahl, Mette","Kampmann, Freja Bach","Friis Bryde Nielsen, Camilla","Lundbergh, Bjørn","Christensen, Rasmus Wibaek","Kårhus, Line Lund","Madsen, Anja Lykke","Hansen, Christian Stevns","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Suetta, Charlotte","Kjaer, Michael","Grarup, Niels","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Larsen, Michael","Køber, Lars","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Loos, Ruth J.F.","Hansen, Torben","Linneberg, Allan","Vaag, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721417"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital","University of California San Francisco"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cardiovascular Diseases prevention control","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 epidemiology","Follow Up Studies","Glucose","Humans","Middle Aged","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for the combined cardiometabolic deep phenotyping and registry based 000000000020 year follow up study of the inter000000000099 cohort","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078501","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721417","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10826573","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38286704","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184011808","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a7f818c8-f801-44f3-9713-f89c44ed44c9"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cardiovascular Diseases/prevention & control","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/epidemiology","Follow-Up Studies","Glucose","Humans","Middle Aged","Registries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2518AA96A2731A4847F2961873AE748E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381240948/e078501.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078501","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Univer