{"abstract":"According to the International Life Saving Federation (ILS), integrating lifeguards in the local or regional emergency medical service (EMS) is a necessity to prevent drowning and improve prehospital treatment in selected situations. This review describes the organisation of lifeguards in Denmark, focusing on essential skills and equipment to assist prehospital EMS in drowning, out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, and search and rescue operations. Standardised requirements for the medical education of lifeguards are warranted to improve prehospital treatment and integration in the EMS.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Oliver Beierholm","Bitzer, Kasper","Mikkelsen, Søren","Collatz Christensen, Helle","Breindahl, Niklas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733801"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Breindahl, Niklas"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["TrygFonden"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"livreddere i danmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/260688905/V05230325_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733801","ids":["sdu-5f629951-a156-4f27-b815-0e08bf7bc3d7"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-754BD042E7D035146440B8B74ECF7AC5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/260688905/V05230325_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/livreddere-i-danmark","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Prehospital Area"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["TrygFonden"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["RKKP"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver Beierholm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"a078a3ac-92b3-4e68-bcd0-983f1a0a3a9f","name":"Sørensen, Oliver Beierholm","orcid":"0009-0004-2028-065X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"bitzerpau","last":"Bitzer","name":"Bitzer, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"7df86a29-c6dc-4919-a9f9-6f5c23591e1d","name":"Mikkelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5187-7027","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"collatzchristensenpau","last":"Collatz Christensen","name":"Collatz Christensen, Helle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"breindahlpau","last":"Breindahl","name":"Breindahl, Niklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"8","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V05230325","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191377582"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","rkkp"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5f629951-a156-4f27-b815-0e08bf7bc3d7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Livreddere i Danmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733801","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: In Denmark, the use of bicycles is widespread, and head injuries are often seen in cyclists involved in collisions. Despite the well-known effects of using a helmet to reduce head injuries, using helmets is not mandatory in Denmark. The primary objective of this study was to provide data regarding injury outcomes and helmet usage. Methods: Participants were bicyclists who sustained head injuries in bicycle collisions and were assessed by the Copenhagen Emergency Medical Services between 1 January 2016; and 15 June 2019. Patients with suspected head injury were identified in an electronic prehospital patient record. Data were linked to the Danish National Patient Registry to retrieve the diagnosis and were categorized into head injury or no head injury based on the diagnosis. Adjusted logistic regression analyses were reported with odds ratios and corresponding confidence intervals to assess the risk of head injury while adjusting for risk factors like age, sex, alcohol consumption, occurrence during weekends and traumatic brain injury. Results: A total of 407 patients were included in this study. Within this entity, 247 (61%) had sustained a head injury. The use of a helmet was reported in one-third of the included patients. Among the head-injured patients, 13% sustained moderate to severe head injuries. Patients with suspected alcohol involvement were significantly less likely to report the use of a helmet. Helmet use reduced the risk of head injury with an odds ratio of 0.52, (95% CI 0.31 − 0.86). In high-energy trauma, the use of a helmet showed a significant reduction in the risk of sustaining a head injury with an odds ratio of 0.28, (95% CI 0.12 − 0.80). Conclusions: In this study, using a helmet was associated with a significantly decreased risk of head injury; this association was even more significant in high-energy trauma.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Beck, Erik Malling","Wolthers, Signe Amalie","Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj","Breindahl, Niklas","Eskesen, Vagn","Lippert, Freddy","Christensen, Helle Collatz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777118"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Head injury","traumatic brain injury TBI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"head injuries related to bicycle collisions and helmet use an observational study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15389588.2024.2363476","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777118","identifier":[{"id":"85196639373","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38905159","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1e32916c-5aa1-401f-a5c1-577cb2ddec13"],"keyword":["Head injury","bicycle collision","helmet","traumatic brain injury (TBI)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-567D9BF3473F8BD1551C57839D8EE327"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411634571/Head_injuries_related_to_bicycle_collisions_and_helmet_use_an_observational_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15389588.2024.2363476","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Emergency Medical Services"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"