, Johanna Sophie","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanna Sophie","key":"buerkertoth","last":"Buerkert","name":"Buerkert, Johanna Sophie","rank":15,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Friis","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"64a86dd8-1629-4f1c-a6d4-def7c2ce880e","name":"Lund, Jens Friis","orcid":"0000-0002-7336-0395","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Friis","key":"lundoth","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Jens Friis","rank":16,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frederik","key":"appelolsenpau","last":"Appel Olsen","locid":"7adf89c7-f58e-48f2-bd0d-4ec36c57edd7","name":"Appel Olsen, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0002-3571-2812","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Appel","key":"olsenoth","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Frederik Appel","rank":17,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["au-19175683-7dc8-45ff-b2bd-1511fab557c6","ku-0653abee-ef5b-4071-b12a-86168d78a899"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selvfølgelig skal KU føre en ambitiøs klimapolitik","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.88-681344","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cardiac arrest following trauma is a leading cause of death, mandating urgent treatment. This study aimed to investigate and compare the incidence, prognostic factors, and survival between patients suffering from traumatic cardiac arrest (TCA) and non-traumatic cardiac arrest (non-TCA). METHODS: This cohort study included all patients suffering from out-of-hospital cardiac arrest in Denmark between 2016 and 2021. TCAs were identified in the prehospital medical record and linked to the out-of-hospital cardiac arrest registry. Descriptive and multivariable analyses were performed with 30-day survival as the primary outcome. RESULTS: A total of 30,215 patients with out-of-hospital cardiac arrests were included. Among those, 984 (3.3%) were TCA. TCA patients were younger and predominantly male (77.5% vs 63.6%, p =  < 0.01) compared to non-TCA patients. Return of spontaneous circulation occurred in 27.3% of cases vs 32.3% in non-TCA patients, p < 0.01, and 30-day survival was 7.3% vs 14.2%, p < 0.01. An initial shockable rhythm was associated with increased survival (aOR = 11.45, 95% CI [6.24 - 21.24] in TCA patients. When comparing TCA with non-TCA other trauma and penetrating trauma were associated with lower survival (aOR: 0.2, 95% CI [0.02-0.54] and aOR: 0.1, 95% CI [0.03 - 0.31], respectively. Non-TCA was associated with an aOR: 3.47, 95% CI [2.53 - 4,91]. CONCLUSION: Survival from TCA is lower than in non-TCA. TCA has different predictors of outcome compared to non-TCA, illustrating the differences regarding the aetiologies of cardiac arrest. Presenting with an initial shockable cardiac rhythm might be associated with a favourable outcome in TCA.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wolthers, Signe Amalie","Jensen, Theo Walther","Breindahl, Niklas","Milling, Louise","Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj","Andersen, Lars Bredevang","Mikkelsen, Søren","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Christensen, Helle Collatz"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-673130"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Wolthers, Signe Amalie"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Emergency Medical Services","Epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest epidemiology","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Registries","Resuscitation","Retrospective Studies","Trauma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"traumatic cardiac arrest a nationwide danish study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12873-023-00839-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish Cardiovascular academy. The funding source had no role in the study design, collection, management, analysis, interpretation of data, writing of the manuscript, or the decision to submit the manuscript for publication. A special thanks to the collaboration group members from the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry Group in the acquisition, analysis, and interpretation of data. All members of the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry validation group are affiliated with The Danish Clinical Quality Program, National Clinical Registries, Copenhagen, Denmark: Gunhild Kjærgaard-Andersen, Louise Milling, Ulrik Havshøj, René Arne Bergmann, Jan Medom Linnebjerg, Michael Boddum, Heinrich Dedenroth Larsen, Theo Walther Jensen, Mathias Geldermann Holgersen, Stig Nikolaj Fasmer Blomberg, Helle Collatz Christensen, Harman Gailand Hassan Yonis, Julie Linding Bogh Kjerulff, Emilie Kabel Madsen, Kristian Bundgaard Ringgren, Dorthe Sofie Haals, Lars Borup, Kenneth Lübcke. This work was supported by the Laerdal Foundation and by the Danish Cardiovascular Academy. The funding sources had no role in the study design, collection, management, analysis, interpretation of data, writing of the manuscript, or the decision to submit the manuscript for publication. This work was supported by the Danish Cardiovascular academy. The funding source had no role in the study design, collection, management, analysis, interpretation of data, writing of the manuscript, or the decision to submit the manuscript for publication. A special thanks to the collaboration group members from the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry Group in the acquisition, analysis, and interpretation of data. All members of the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry validation group are affiliated with The Danish Clinical Quality Program, National Clinical Registries, Copenhagen, Denmark: Gunhild Kjærgaard-Andersen, Louise Milling, Ulrik Havshøj, René Arne Bergmann, Jan Medom Linnebjerg, Michael Boddum, Heinrich Dedenroth Larsen, Theo Walther Jensen, Mathias Geldermann Holgersen, Stig Nikolaj Fasmer Blomberg, Helle Collatz Christensen, Harman Gailand Hassan Yonis, Julie Linding Bogh Kjerulff, Emilie Kabel Madsen, Kristian Bundgaard Ringgren, Dorthe Sofie Haals, Lars Borup, Kenneth Lübcke."],"id":"S02-099.94-673130","identifier":[{"id":"37340347","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10283219","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85162873963","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-821f7db6-e28d-4954-bd75-b43884e09bf7","sdu-bb05ebe3-426f-4a2c-a2bb-4daf2ec43a7f"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation/adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Emergency Medical Services","Epidemiology","Female","Humans","Male","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/epidemiology","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Prehospital interventions","Registries","Resuscitation","Retrospective Studies","Trauma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7027A3BB1479F60E785A44218C552E91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12873-023-00839-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/358330298/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/235416913/s12873_023_00839_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Prehospital Area"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Region of Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg","Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Signe Amalie","key":"woltherspau","last":"Wolthers","name":"Wolthers, Signe Amalie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Theo Walther","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Theo Walther","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"breindahlpau","last":"Breindahl","name":"Breindahl, Niklas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"millingpau","last":"Milling","locid":"e190eca7-5826-456c-bb1e-f41f8e431770","name":"Milling, Louise","orcid":"0000-0001-8320-5391","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Stig Nikolaj","key":"blombergpau","last":"Blomberg","locid":"5a3912f5-540e-4f29-a5c6-5f28d1327eb0","name":"Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lars Bredevang","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lars Bredevang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"7df86a29-c6dc-4919-a9f9-6f5c23591e1d","name":"Mikkelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5187-7027","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"f71bedc6-3736-4559-b937-6a18e770616e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Helle Collatz","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b05bae82-5e32-4f10-980c-147b4af03d6a","name":"Christensen, Helle Collatz","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37340347"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12873-023-00839-1","issn":["1471227X"],"journal":"BMC Emergency Medicine","paperid":"69","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Emergency Medicine","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162873963"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-821f7db6-e28d-4954-bd75-b43884e09bf7","sdu-bb05ebe3-426f-4a2c-a2bb-4daf2ec43a7f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Traumatic cardiac arrest - a nationwide Danish study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-673130","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: This study aimed to compare hospital admission and 30-day mortality between patients assessed by the prehospital assessment unit (PAU) and patients not assessed by the PAU. DESIGN: This was a matched cohort study. SETTING: This study was conducted between November 2021 and October 2022 in Region Zealand, Denmark. PARTICIPANTS: 989 patients aged >18, assessed by the PAU, were identified, and 9860 patients not assessed by the PAU were selected from the emergency calls using exposure density sampling. EXPOSURE: Patients assessed by the PAU. The PAU is operated by paramedics with access to point-of-care test facilities. The PAU is an alternative response vehicle without the capability of transporting patients. PRIMARY AND SECONDARY OUTCOME MEASURES: The primary outcome was hospital admission within 48 hours after the initial call. The key secondary outcomes were admission within 7 days, 30-day mortality and admission within 6 hours. Descriptive statistical analyses were conducted, and logistic regression models were used to estimate adjusted OR (aOR) and 95% CI. RESULTS: Among the PAU assessed, 44.1% were admitted within 48 hours, compared with 72.9% of the non-PAU assessed, p<0.001. The multivariable analysis showed a lower risk of admission within 48 hours and 7 days among the PAU patients, aOR 0.31 (95% CI 0.26 to 0.38) and aOR 0.50 (95% CI 0.38 to 0.64), respectively. The 30-day mortality rate was 3.8% in the PAU-assessed patients vs 5.5% in the non-PAU-assessed patients, p=0.03. In the multivariable analysis, no significant difference was found in mortality aOR 0.99 (95% CI 0.71 to 1.42). No deaths were observed in PAU-assessed patients without subsequent follow-up. CONCLUSION: The recently introduced PAU aims for patient-centred emergency care. The PAU-assessed patients had reduced admissions within 48 hours and 7 days after the initial call. Study findings indicate that the PAU is safe since we identified no significant differences in 30-day mortality. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05654909.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wolthers, Signe Amalie","Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj Fasmer","Breindahl, Niklas","Anjum, Sair","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Andersen, Lars Bredevang","Christensen, Helle Collatz"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716461"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Wolthers, Signe Amalie"],"keyword":["Cohort Studies","Emergency Medical Services","Epidemiology","Hospitalization","Hospitals","Humans","Patient Centered Care","Public health"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Prehospital Center, Region Zealand, Næstved"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between using a prehospital assessment unit and hospital admission and mortality a matched cohort study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-075592","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study recieved funding from Region Sjællands Sundhedsvidenskabelige Forskningsfond."],"id":"S02-100.00-716461","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10533654","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85172425095","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37739475","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-92a6bb7f-b9ac-4f6a-909b-7458a2419b7d","sdu-728d919f-0b5d-452c-8007-5348636c7a8f"],"keyword":["Cohort Studies","EPIDEMIOLOGY","Emergency Medical Services","Hospitalization","Hospitals","Humans","PUBLIC HEALTH","Patient-Centered Care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A116D37D0156C3BEAC97FF9E4463639A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":