envictorpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"2c41303f-cdcc-4466-b53e-e80b2ebe8b1f","name":"Sørensen, Victor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Eva Wulff","key":"helgeevawulffpau","last":"Helge","locid":"9bcf2b77-54e8-41d5-b356-d93a8350899b","name":"Helge, Eva Wulff","orcid":"0000-0002-4351-0137","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Maja Kjærgaard","key":"christensenmajakjærgaardpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"58a0b029-8a71-4672-882c-2d8d57cfba0b","name":"Christensen, Maja Kjærgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Julie Boye","key":"kjærgaardjulieboyepau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"60340df9-6afa-43e8-a165-da153379319f","name":"Kjærgaard, Julie Boye","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Kjeldgaard","key":"møllertrinekjeldgaardpau","last":"Møller","locid":"82f50dde-cd8e-4756-8d80-66c3a7b981e6","name":"Møller, Trine Kjeldgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8337-9575","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jørn Wulff","key":"helgejørnwulffpau","last":"Helge","locid":"a5560afa-4f31-4278-8ae9-0c49fb0027c1","name":"Helge, Jørn Wulff","orcid":"0000-0001-9724-5423","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael","key":"rørthmikaelpau","last":"Rørth","locid":"f279398e-9773-4d96-be8a-832d3de47825","name":"Rørth, Mikael","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Eva Soelberg","key":"vadstrupevasoelbergpau","last":"Vadstrup","name":"Vadstrup, Eva Soelberg","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"krustruppeterpau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"466150ff-704b-461f-8004-692635d9c82b","name":"Krustrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1461-9838","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33794005"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sms.13963","issn":["09057188","16000838"],"issn_org":["09057188"],"issue":"7","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","pages":"1545-1557","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104119485"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-385a83d7-cb9c-4749-836e-9857f2bc0598","kp-29882a6b-5731-4ab7-8db7-7516761ee969","ku-0ec70b77-b528-4503-ab78-b01d79d9829e","sdu-951064f8-465c-4693-aea5-351057dd0ee1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"One year of Football Fitness improves L1–L4 BMD, postural balance, and muscle strength in women treated for breast cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.78-016778","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hypothermia or Normothermia after Cardiac Arrest This trial randomly assigned patients with coma after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest to undergo targeted hypothermia at 33 degrees C or normothermia with treatment of fever. At 6 months, there were no significant between-group differences regarding death or functional outcomes. Background Targeted temperature management is recommended for patients after cardiac arrest, but the supporting evidence is of low certainty. Methods In an open-label trial with blinded assessment of outcomes, we randomly assigned 1900 adults with coma who had had an out-of-hospital cardiac arrest of presumed cardiac or unknown cause to undergo targeted hypothermia at 33 degrees C, followed by controlled rewarming, or targeted normothermia with early treatment of fever (body temperature, >= 37.8 degrees C). The primary outcome was death from any cause at 6 months. Secondary outcomes included functional outcome at 6 months as assessed with the modified Rankin scale. Prespecified subgroups were defined according to sex, age, initial cardiac rhythm, time to return of spontaneous circulation, and presence or absence of shock on admission. Prespecified adverse events were pneumonia, sepsis, bleeding, arrhythmia resulting in hemodynamic compromise, and skin complications related to the temperature management device. Results A total of 1850 patients were evaluated for the primary outcome. At 6 months, 465 of 925 patients (50%) in the hypothermia group had died, as compared with 446 of 925 (48%) in the normothermia group (relative risk with hypothermia, 1.04; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.94 to 1.14; P=0.37). Of the 1747 patients in whom the functional outcome was assessed, 488 of 881 (55%) in the hypothermia group had moderately severe disability or worse (modified Rankin scale score >= 4), as compared with 479 of 866 (55%) in the normothermia group (relative risk with hypothermia, 1.00; 95% CI, 0.92 to 1.09). Outcomes were consistent in the prespecified subgroups. Arrhythmia resulting in hemodynamic compromise was more common in the hypothermia group than in the normothermia group (24% vs. 17%, P Conclusions In patients with coma after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, targeted hypothermia did not lead to a lower incidence of death by 6 months than targeted normothermia. (Funded by the Swedish Research Council and others; TTM2 ClinicalTrials.gov number, .)","author_count":55,"contributors":["Dankiewicz, Josef","Cronberg, Tobias","Lilja, Gisela","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Levin, Helena","Ullén, Susann","Rylander, Christian","Wise, Matt P","Oddo, Mauro","Cariou, Alain","Bělohlávek, Jan","Hovdenes, Jan","Saxena, Manoj","Kirkegaard, Hans","Young, Paul J","Pelosi, Paolo","Storm, Christian","Taccone, Fabio S","Joannidis, Michael","Callaway, Clifton","Eastwood, Glenn M","Morgan, Matt P G","Nordberg, Per","Erlinge, David","Nichol, Alistair D","Chew, Michelle S","Hollenberg, Jacob","Thomas, Matthew","Bewley, Jeremy","Sweet, Katie","Grejs, Anders M","Christensen, Steffen","Haenggi, Matthias","Levis, Anja","Lundin, Andreas","Düring, Joachim","Schmidbauer, Simon","Keeble, Thomas R","Karamasis, Grigoris V","Schrag, Claudia","Faessler, Edith","Smid, Ondrej","Otáhal, Michal","Maggiorini, Marco","Wendel Garcia, Pedro D","Jaubert, Paul","Cole, Jade M","Solar, Miroslav","Borgquist, Ola","Nielsen, Niklas","Lange, Theis"],"cuid":["S02-096.21-047416"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["TTM2 Trial Invest","TTM2 Trial Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Niklas"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Czechia","France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Malaysia","New Zealand","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Cantonal Hospital St. Gallen","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Charles University","Free University of Brussels","General University Hospital in Prague","Helsingborg Hospital","IRCCS Ospedale Policlinico San Martino","Innsbruck Medical University","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","Monash University","Monash University Malaysia","Oslo University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","South Western Sydney Local Hlth Dist, Bankstown Lidcombe Hosp","Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics","Univ Bern, University of Bern, University Hospital of Bern, Bern Univ Hosp, Dept Anesthesiol & Pain Med, Inselspital","Univ Bern, University of Bern, University Hospital of Bern, Bern Univ Hosp, Dept Intens Care Med","Univ Coll Dublin, University College Dublin, Clin Res Ctr, St Vincents Univ Hosp","Univ Hosp Zurich, Inst Intens Care Med","University Hospital of Wales","University of Gothenburg","University of Pittsburgh","Wellington Hosp, Medical Research Institute Of New Zealand, Med Res Inst New Zealand, Intens Care Unit"],"keyword":["Aged","American Heart Association","Body Temperature","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation methods","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Coma etiology","European Resuscitation Council","Female","Fever etiology","Guidelines","Humans","Hypothermia Induced adverse effects","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest complications","Single Blind Method","Targeted temperature management","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Univ Hosp Wales, Cardiff University, Adult Crit Care"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypothermia versus normothermia after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","