All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-574463e8-041b-4780-99a9-c5f309f1fead","ku-39e19360-e15e-40b6-8879-3706832be4a2","sdu-9827f655-4d13-49c6-8b79-3755b3bd28a6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of Metformin vs. Placebo in Combination with Insulin Analogues on Bone Markers P1NP and CTX in Patients with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-004263","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Fibrin-d-dimer (d-dimer) is essential for the diagnosis and treatment of thrombosis patients. The new ACL TOP 50- series used for d-dimer determination, integrates a preanalytical interference check for hemolysis, icterus and lipemia (HIL-test). Using earlier versions of ACL TOP, HIL was evaluated by visual inspection by the biomedical laboratory scientist. With the new integrated HIL-test, lipemia is determined by measuring turbidity in the sample at 671 nm, reflecting the lipid content in the sample. Using the new ACL TOP 50- series, we observed more samples being rejected for d-dimer analysis due to lipemia-interference evaluated by the integrated HIL-test suggesting a discrepancy between the former triglyceride-based cut-off and the new turbidity-based cut-off. Therefore, to re-evaluate the lipemia interference cut-off with the turbidimetric measurement, we did a spike-in experiment, using intralipid as lipemia simulation. Three × six different patient pools were prepared from sodium-citrate plasma. We observed no interference in the d-dimer assay by intralipid concentrations resulting in milli absorbances (mAbs) below 3000 mAbs. Thus, the cut-off for lipemia interference using the integrated HIL-test on ACL TOP 550 should be 3000 mAbs. This cut-off will reduce the number of samples rejected due to false positive interference and at the same time reduce 'hands on' time for the biomedical laboratory scientists and minimize the risk of subjective evaluation by a visual inspection.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Annette Klug","Christensen, Gitte Lund","Dalgård, Anette","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye"],"cuid":["S02-094.74-042974"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Niklas Rye"],"keyword":["Automation Laboratory","Fibrin Fibrinogen Degradation Products analysis","Hemolysis","Humans","Lipemia","Preanalytical","Thrombosis","Triglyceride","Triglycerides blood"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of lipemia interference with automated hil test on d dimer acl top 000000000050 series analysis reveals a higher cut off than manufacturer s recommendations","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85076922046","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.74-042974","identifier":[{"id":"31846357","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85076922046","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-637a701c-3f3b-4ce5-950f-270df1755977","sdu-249020a2-4348-4a95-ac76-b38f6c3802a7"],"keyword":["Automation, Laboratory","Fibrin Fibrinogen Degradation Products/analysis","Hematologic Tests/instrumentation","Hemolysis","Humans","Hyperlipidemias/blood","Lipemia","Nephelometry and Turbidimetry","Triglycerides/blood","fibrin d dimer","preanalytical","thrombosis","triglyceride"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9D0766182CCE99A3828FBC2FB7F8619E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette Klug","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Annette Klug","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Lund","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Gitte Lund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"dalgårdpau","last":"Dalgård","name":"Dalgård, Anette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31846357"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365513.2019.1703214","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"168-171","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076922046"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-637a701c-3f3b-4ce5-950f-270df1755977","sdu-249020a2-4348-4a95-ac76-b38f6c3802a7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Estimation of lipemia interference with automated HIL-test on d-dimer ACL TOP 50 series analysis : reveals a higher cut-off than manufacturer's recommendations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.74-042974","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background Intravenous high-dose glucagon is a recommended antidote against beta-blocker poisonings, but clinical effects are unclear. We therefore investigated hemodynamic effects and safety of high-dose glucagon with and without concomitant beta-blockade. Methods and Results In a randomized crossover study, 10 healthy men received combinations of esmolol (1.25 mg/kg bolus+0.75 mg/kg/min infusion), glucagon (50 µg/kg), and identical volumes of saline placebo on 5 separate days in random order (saline+saline; esmolol+saline; esmolol+glucagon bolus; saline+glucagon infusion; saline+glucagon bolus). On individual days, esmolol/saline was infused from -15 to 30 minutes. Glucagon/saline was administered from 0 minutes as a 2-minute intravenous bolus or as a 30-minute infusion (same total glucagon dose). End points were hemodynamic and adverse effects of glucagon compared with saline. Compared with saline, glucagon bolus increased mean heart rate by 13.0 beats per minute (95% CI, 8.0-18.0; P<0.001), systolic blood pressure by 15.6 mm Hg (95% CI, 8.0-23.2; P=0.002), diastolic blood pressure by 9.4 mm Hg (95% CI, 6.3-12.6; P<0.001), and cardiac output by 18.0 % (95% CI, 9.7-26.9; P=0.003) at the 5-minute time point on days without beta-blockade. Similar effects of glucagon bolus occurred on days with beta-blockade and between 15 and 30 minutes during infusion. Hemodynamic effects of glucagon thus reflected pharmacologic glucagon plasma concentrations. Glucagon-induced nausea occurred in 80% of participants despite ondansetron pretreatment. Conclusions High-dose glucagon boluses had significant hemodynamic effects regardless of beta-blockade. A glucagon infusion had comparable and apparently longer-lasting effects compared with bolus, indicating that infusion may be preferable to bolus injections. Registration Information URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT03533179.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Petersen, Kasper M.","Bøgevig, Søren","Riis, Troels","Andersson, Niklas W.","Dalhoff, Kim","Holst, Jens Juul","Knop, Filip K.","Faber, Jens","Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","Christensen, Mikkel Bring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544938"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beta blocker","Glucagon","Hemodynamics","Toxicology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high dose glucagon has hemodynamic effects regardless of cardiac beta adrenoceptor blockade a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.120.016828","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-544938","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7763418","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85095666358","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000588373500003","type":"wos"},{"id":"33103603","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fde7fa71-543a-411f-b713-88d95d2ae7e4"],"keyword":["beta blocker","glucagon","hemodynamics","toxicology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F80AA423E13941AF483E438D254A3920"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.120.016828","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251639990/JAHA.120.016828.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kasper M.","key":"petersenkaspermpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Kasper M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren","key":"bøgevigsørenpau","last":"Bøgevig","name":"Bøgevig, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Troels","key":"riistroelspau","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Troels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niklas W.","key":"anderssonniklaswpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Niklas W.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim P.","key":"dalhoffkimpau","last":"Dalhoff","locid":"1bacc939-23ea-4041-9815-4d3b92b6d9c3","name":"Dalhoff, Kim","name_org":"Dalhoff, Kim P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip K.","key":"knopfilipkpau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"faberjenspau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tonny S.","key":"petersentonnystudsgaardpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"95e21f85-7cd9-443d-88c7-cc0b6e7bc844","name":"Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","name_org":"Petersen, Tonny S.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel B.","key":"christensenmikkelbringpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"4f5c91e2-3caa-4263-8d9c-df3bfdfbd31b","name":"Christensen, Mikkel Bring","name_org":"Christensen, Mikkel B.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33103603"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.120.016828","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"21","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e016828","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85095666358"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fde7fa71-543a-411f-b713-88d95d2ae7e4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-Dose Glucagon Has Hemodynamic Effects Regardless of Cardiac Beta-Adrenoceptor Blockade : A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-544938","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This article presents a collection of short testimonies and workspace photographs received between 18 March and 5 May in response to my Call for Testimonies reproduced in the next section. The testimonies are lined up in order of when they were received. Each section starts with the place and time of writing, followed by a brief author biography, their testimony, and one workspace photograph. In numbers, the collection consists of 81 textual testimonies and 80 workspace photographs submitted by 84 authors from 19 countries: USA (13), UK (11), China (9), India (7), Australia (7), New Zealand (7), Denmark (6), Sweden (6), Croatia (5), Canada (2), Spain (2), Nigeria (2), Finland (2), Ireland (2), Malta (1), Tanzania (1), Malaysia (1), Latvia (1), and South Africa (1). As it is common in the academia, many authors are expats and carry multiple identities; the collection reflects places of writing their testimonies rather than places of their origin.","author_count":84,"contributors":["Jandrić, Petar","Hayes, David","Truelove, Ian","Levinson, Paul","Mayo, Peter","Ryberg, Thomas","Monzó, Lilia D.","Allen, Quaylan","Stewart, Paul Alexander","Carr, Paul R.","Jackson, Liz","Bridges, Susan","Escaño, Carlos","Grauslund, Dennis","Mañero, Julia","Lukoko, Happiness Onesmo","Bryant, Peter","Fuentes-Martinez, Ana","Gibbons, Andrew","Sturm, Sean","Rose, Jennifer","Chuma, Mohamed Muhibu","Biličić, Eva","Pfohl, Sarah","Gustafsson, Ulrika","Arantes, Janine Aldous","Ford, Derek R.","Kihwele, Jimmy Ezekiel","Mozelius, Peter","Suoranta, Juha","Jurjević, Lucija","Jurčević, Matija","Steketee, Anne","Irwin, Jones","White, E. Jayne","Davidsen, Jacob","Jaldemark, Jimmy","Abegglen, Sandra","Burns, Tom","Sinfield, Sandra","Kirylo, James D.","Kokić, Ivana Batarelo","Stewart, Georgina Tuari","Rikowski, Glenn","Christensen, Line Lisberg","Arndt, Sonja","Pyyhtinen, Olli","Reitz, Charles","Lodahl, Mikkel","Humble, Niklas","Buchanan, Rachel","Forster, Daniella J.","Kishore, Pallavi","Ozol