{"abstract":"CONTEXT: The gut-derived incretin hormones glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) and glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) have been suggested to play a role in bone metabolism. Exogenous administration of GIP inhibits bone resorption, but the effect of GLP-1 is less clear. Furthermore, the combined effect of exogenous GIP and GLP-1 on bone metabolism is unknown. OBJECTIVE: To investigate the effect of separate and combined infusions of the incretin hormones GIP and GLP-1 on bone resorption and formation. DESIGN: Randomized, double-blinded, placebo-controlled, crossover study including five study days. PARTICIPANTS: Seventeen overweight/obese men. INTERVENTIONS: On the first study day, a 50-g oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) was performed. On the next four study days, isoglycemic IV glucose infusions (IIGI), mimicking the glucose excursions from the OGTT, were performed with concomitant infusions of GIP (4 pmol/kg/min), GLP-1 (1 pmol/kg/min), GIP+GLP-1 (4 and 1 pmol/kg/min, respectively), or placebo, respectively. PRIMARY OUTCOMES: Changes in bone resorption assessed by measurements of carboxy-terminal type I collagen crosslinks (CTX) and in bone formation as assessed by procollagen type 1 N-terminal propeptide (P1NP) concentrations. RESULTS: During the OGTT, CTX was significantly lowered by 54 ± 13% from baseline (mean ± SD) compared with 28 ± 12% during IIGI + saline (P < 0.0001). During IIGI+GLP-1 and IIGI+GIP, CTX was lowered by 65 ± 16% and 74 ± 9%, respectively, from baseline, whereas IGII+GIP+GLP-1 lowered CTX by 84 ± 4% from baseline. P1NP levels were unaffected by the interventions. CONCLUSIONS: Our data suggest that GLP-1, like GIP, may be involved in regulation of bone resorption and that GIP and GLP-1 together have partially additive inhibitory effects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bergmann, Natasha C","Lund, Asger","Gasbjerg, Lærke S.","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Jessen, Lene","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Christensen, Mikkel Bring","Vilsbøll, Tina","Knop, Filip K."],"cuid":["S02-099.78-042394"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Department of In Vivo Pharmacology, Zealand Pharma A/S, Glostrup, Denmark."],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"separate and combined effects of gip and glp 000000000001 infusions on bone metabolism in overweight men without diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85067197247","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.78-042394","identifier":[{"id":"85067197247","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30848791","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-51669376-7249-499c-9b22-6ed5375a14e2","sdu-dba75ac2-9602-46ed-8b40-10dda5875a16"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-451002C5AC46327A381A4D49C26AB4B2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of In Vivo Pharmacology, Zealand Pharma A/S, Glostrup, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"zealand pharma","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ZEA","l3nl":"Zealand Pharma A/S","l3nn":"Zealand Pharma","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Zealand Pharma","namevar":["Zealand Pharma"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Natasha Chidekel","key":"bergmannpau","last":"Bergmann","locid":"a7216d77-f29e-489b-bf4d-1bf85769c615","name":"Bergmann, Natasha C","name_org":"Bergmann, Natasha Chidekel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Asger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lærke Smidt","key":"gasbjergpau","last":"Gasbjerg","locid":"38691fd4-0b1c-4371-b423-954525f5f9b3","name":"Gasbjerg, Lærke S.","name_org":"Gasbjerg, Lærke Smidt","orcid":"0000-0002-7880-8515","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Lene","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","name":"Jessen, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Bring","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"4f5c91e2-3caa-4263-8d9c-df3bfdfbd31b","name":"Christensen, Mikkel Bring","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina","key":"vilsbøllpau","last":"Vilsbøll","locid":"76773372-af8c-45a0-9447-a509cbf6d466","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-0456-6787","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip Krag","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Filip Krag","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30848791"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2019-00008","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"2953-2960","publisher":"Endocrine Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067197247"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","Zealand Pharma A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-51669376-7249-499c-9b22-6ed5375a14e2","sdu-dba75ac2-9602-46ed-8b40-10dda5875a16"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Separate and Combined Effects of GIP and GLP-1 Infusions on Bone Metabolism in Overweight Men Without Diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.78-042394","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Summary: Given that bone turnover markers are often shipped to central laboratories, it is essential to be aware of factors that will affect stability. We have evaluated how sample type, time before separation of blood samples, and time between separation and analysis affect the stability of four bone turnover markers. Introduction: Bone turnover markers are often shipped to central laboratories for analysis, which require knowledge of the stability of the markers of interest in different sample materials. The aim of the current study was to evaluate how time before separation of blood samples and time between separation and analysis affect the stability of four bone turnover markers in serum and plasma samples. Methods: Serum, EDTA, and Lithium heparin (LiHep) plasma samples from seven osteoporosis patients and three healthy controls were collected and stored at room temperature for up to 72 h before separation and analysis. After separation, samples were stored at room temperature for up to 72 h and re-analyzed. The bone turnover markers N-terminal pro-collagen type 1 extension pro-peptide (P1NP), bone-specific alkaline phosphatase (BAP), C-terminal teleopeptide cross links of collagen type 1 (CTX), and osteocalcin (OC) were analyzed using the automated iSYS IDS platform. Results: P1NP and BAP were stable in both plasma and serum for 72 h before centrifugation. CTX levels were higher in EDTA plasma at all time points compared to LiHep plasma and serum. The use of EDTA plasma prolonged the stability of CTX as compared to LiHep plasma and serum. Osteocalcin showed high tendency to degrade in all sample types and concentrations were significantly lower after 24 h of storage. Conclusions: For the bone turnover markers P1NP and BAP, the use of both plasma and serum is recommended. Samples for CTX analysis should be taken as EDTA plasma. Samples for osteocalcin analysis can be taken in either type of plasma or serum, but should be analyzed within 3 h or preserved at − 18 °C.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, G L","Halgreen, J R","Milenkovski, M","Köse, A","Quardon, N","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye"],"cuid":["S02-088.99-043600"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Niklas Rye"],"keyword":["Alkaline Phosphatase blood","Biomarkers blood","Blood Specimen Collection methods","Bone Remodeling physiology","Bone turnover markers","CTX","Case Control Studies","Collagen Type I blood","Humans","Osteocalcin","Osteocalcin blood","Osteoporosis blood","P1NP","Peptide Fragments blood","Peptides blood","Pre analytical","Procollagen blood","Reproducibility of Results","Stability"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone turnover markers are differentially affected by pre analytical handling","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85060647230","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.99-043600","identifier":[{"id":"30680430","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85060647230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-784db92f-1940-4102-807e-b96e24710809","sdu-086da47b-1487-4e29-80b5-ce690b5aeb88"],"keyword":["Alkaline Phosphatase/blood","BAP","Biomarkers/blood","Blood Specimen Collection/methods","Bone Remodeling/physiology","Bone turnover markers","CTX","Case-Control Studies","Collagen Type I/blood","Humans","Osteocalcin","Osteocalcin/blood","Osteoporosis/blood","P1NP","Peptide Fragments/blood","Peptides/blood","Pre-analytical","Procollagen/blood","Reproducibility of Results","Stability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BC015EB6D2FCE72529BBDB79E2032AC5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G. L.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, G. L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J R","key":"halgreenpau","last":"Halgreen","name":"Halgreen, J R","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M","key":"milenkovskipau","last":"Milenkovski","name":"Milenkovski, M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A","key":"kösepau","last":"Köse","name":"Köse, A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"N","key":"quardonpau","last":"Quardon","name":"Quardon, N","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"N R","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jørgensen, N R","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30680430"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00198-019-04837-7","issn":["0937941X","14332965"],"issn_org":["0937941X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Osteoporosis International","pages":"1137-1141","status":"p","title":"Osteoporosis International","title_org":"Osteoporosis international : a journal established as result of cooperation between the European Foundation for Osteoporosis and the National Osteoporosis Foundation of the USA","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060647230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-784db92f-1940-4102-807e-b96e24710809","sdu-086da47b-1487-4e29-80b5-ce690b5aeb88"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bone turnover markers are differentially affected by pre-analytical handling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.99-043600","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Gitte Høj","Fox, Anthony David","Christensen, Thomas Kjær","Clausen, Preben","Koffijberg, Kees","Liljebäck, Niklas","Mitchell, Carl","Nilsson, Leif","Alhainen, Mikko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-169630"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Sovon Dutch Centre for Field Ornithology","Wildfowl and Wetlands Trust"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"taiga bean goose population status report 000000002017 000000002018","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.unep-aewa.org/en/document/taiga-bean-goose-population-status-report-2017-2018","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-169630","ids":["au-46a9a93a-2334-4c71-be08-8c83f30e632f"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3CEF5E063833B84698F5244167F7AB4E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Wildlife Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"sovon dutch centre for field ornithology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sovon Dutch Centre for Field Ornithology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"wildfowl and wetlands trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Wildfowl and Wetlands Trust","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Høj","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"2c200c35-1b42-4369-a1f0-994e10967abe","name":"Jensen, Gitte Høj","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anthony David","key":"foxpau","last":"Fox","locid":"deb15e30-223d-4759-b62b-1df46dcf0d62","name":"Fox, Anthony David","orcid":"0000-0001-8083-7633","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Kjær","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5554437a-52ef-4f5b-a1e8-7f22fbec1bee","name":"Christensen, Thomas Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Preben","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"09884c6f-eeec-4774-a4e9-db625c26dd82","name":"Clausen, Preben","orcid":"0000-0001-8986-294X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kees","key":"koffijbergpau","last":"Koffijberg","name":"Koffijberg, Kees","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas","key":"liljebäckpau","last":"Liljebäck","name":"Liljebäck, Niklas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl","key":"mitchellpau","last":"Mitchell","name":"Mitchell, Carl","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Leif","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Leif","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"alhainenpau","last":"Alhainen","name":"Alhainen, Mikko","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"11","publisher":"AEWA European Goose Management Platform Data Centre","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-46a9a93a-2334-4c71-be08-8c83f30e632f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Taiga Bean Goose: Population status report 2017-2018","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-169630","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Charcot foot is a rare but severe complication to diabetes and peripheral neuropathy. It is still unclear if an acute Charcot foot has long-term effects on the bone metabolism. To investigate this, we conducted a follow-up study to examine if a previously acute Charcot foot has any long-term effects on bone mineral density (BMD) or local or systemic bone metabolism. METHODS: An 8.5-year follow-up case-control study of 44 individuals with diabetes mellitus, 24 of whom also had acute or chronic Charcot foot at the baseline visit in 2005-2007, who were followed up in 2015 with DXA scans and blood samples. RESULTS: 21 of the 44 baseline participants participated in the follow-up. There were no difference in the change in total hip BMD from baseline to follow-up in either the Charcot or the control group (p = 0.402 and 0.517), and no increased risk of osteoporosis in the previous Charcot feet either. From baseline to follow-up, there was a significant difference in the change in levels of fsRANK-L in the Charcot group, but not in the control group (p = 0.002 and 0.232, respectively). At follow-up, there were no differences in fsRANK-L between the groups. The fsRANK-L/OPG ratio also significantly decreased from baseline to follow-up in the Charcot group (3.4 versus 0.5) (p = 0.009), but not in the control group (1.3 versus 1.1) (p = 0.302). CONCLUSION: We found that diabetes patients with an acute Charcot foot have an elevated fsRANK-L/OPG ratio, and that the level decreased from baseline to follow-up to be comparable to the level in diabetes patients without previous or current Charcot foot. We found no permanent effect of an acute Charcot foot on hip or foot BMD.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jansen, Rasmus Bo","Christensen, Tomas Møller","Bülow, Jens","Rørdam, Lene","Holstein, Per E","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Svendsen, Ole Lander"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-046320"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bone markers","Bone mineral density","Charcot foot","Diabetes mellitus","Journal Article","Neuropathy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone mineral density and markers of bone turnover and inflammation in diabetes patients with or without a charcot foot an 000000000008 000000000005 year prospective case control study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134672161/Bone_mineral_density_and_markers_of_bone_turnover_and_inflammation_in_diabetes_patients_with_or_without_a_Charcot_foot.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-046320","identifier":[{"id":"29196119","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85036529006","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cea6d599-df37-4473-9e88-4b8576bc3962","sdu-fd5d886b-c27e-4b42-a723-19dabc2282b7"],"keyword":["Bone markers","Bone mineral density","Charcot foot","Diabetes mellitus","Journal Article","Neuropathy","RANK-L"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F488ECB9639101D78E8F178D2DFC778B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/134672161/Bone_mineral_density_and_markers_of_bone_turnover_and_inflammation_in_diabetes_patients_with_or_without_a_Charcot_foot.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["​Bispebjerg Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Torekov Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Rasmus Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomas Møller","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Tomas Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jens","key":"bülowpau","last":"Bülow","locid":"0126f721-05d2-4ce9-8c25-20b41eb01f9a","name":"Bülow, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-3921-4888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"rørdampau","last":"Rørdam","name":"Rørdam, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per E","key":"holsteinpau","last":"Holstein","name":"Holstein, Per E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Ole Lander","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"a4602320-eec3-42f0-b4c6-450bf439b1fd","name":"Svendsen, Ole Lander","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29196119"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2017.11.004","issn":["10568727","1873460X"],"issn_org":["10568727"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Diabetes and its Complications","pages":"164-170","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Diabetes and its Complications","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85036529006"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cea6d599-df37-4473-9e88-4b8576bc3962","sdu-fd5d886b-c27e-4b42-a723-19dabc2282b7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bone mineral density and markers of bone turnover and inflammation in diabetes patients with or without a Charcot foot : An 8.5-year prospective case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-046320","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Context: The gut hormone glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) causes postprandial insulin release and inhibits bone resorption assessed by carboxy-terminal collagen crosslinks (CTX). Objective: To study if GIP affects bone homeostasis biomarkers independently of insulin release and glycemic level. Design: Randomized, double-blinded, crossover study with 5 study days. Patients: Ten male C-peptide-negative patients with type 1 diabetes. Interventions: On 3 matched days with \"low glycemia\" (plasma glucose in the interval 3 to 7 mmol/L for 120 minutes), we administered intravenous (IV) GIP (4 pmol × kg-1 × min-1), glucagon-like peptide 1 (1 pmol × kg-1 × min-1), or placebo (saline), and on 2 matched days with \"high glycemia\" (plasma glucose 12 mmol/L for 90 minutes), we administered either GIP or saline. Main Outcome Measures: CTX, procollagen type 1 N-terminal propeptide (P1NP), and parathyroid hormone (PTH). Results: During low glycemia: GIP progressively suppressed CTX from baseline by up to 59 ± 18% compared with 24 ± 10% during saline infusion (P < 0.0001). Absolute values of P1NP and PTH did not differ between days. During high glycemia: GIP suppressed CTX from baseline by up to 59 ± 19% compared with 7 ± 9% during saline infusion (P < 0.0001). P1NP did not differ between days. GIP suppressed PTH after 60 minutes compared with saline (P < 0.01), but this difference disappeared after 90 minutes. Conclusions: Short-term GIP infusions robustly reduce bone resorption independently of endogenous insulin secretion and during both elevated and low plasma glucose, but have no effect on P1NP or PTH after 90 minutes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christensen, Mikkel Bring","Lund, Asger","Calanna, Salvatore","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Holst, Jens Juul","Vilsbøll, Tina","Knop, Filip K."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-046357"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Mikkel B."],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers metabolism","Blood Glucose metabolism","Bone Resorption drug therapy","C Peptide blood","Cross Over Studies","Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 complications","Double Blind Method","Follow Up Studies","Gastrointestinal Agents therapeutic use","Humans","Hypoglycemia etiology","Journal Article","Male","Postprandial Period","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glucose dependent insulinotropic polypeptide gip inhibits bone resorption independently of insulin and glycemia","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85041464998","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-046357","identifier":[{"id":"29099978","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85041464998","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cff6fe60-0b54-4c4b-b70b-d53ccdcac912","sdu-4432bc9b-4213-4021-9302-f97eb103e960"],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers/metabolism","Blood Glucose/metabolism","Bone Resorption/drug therapy","C-Peptide/blood","Cross-Over Studies","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1/complications","Double-Blind Method","Follow-Up Studies","Gastric Inhibitory Polypeptide/therapeutic use","Gastrointestinal Agents/therapeutic use","Humans","Hyperglycemia/etiology","Hypoglycemia/etiology","Journal Article","Male","Postprandial Period","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BDF5BC371551FF41A67A8A44945BD353"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel B","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"4f5c91e2-3caa-4263-8d9c-df3bfdfbd31b","name":"Christensen, Mikkel Bring","name_org":"Christensen, Mikkel B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Asger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Salvatore","key":"calannapau","last":"Calanna","name":"Calanna, Salvatore","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","first":"Niklas R","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jørgensen, Niklas R","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tina","key":"vilsbøllpau","last":"Vilsbøll","locid":"76773372-af8c-45a0-9447-a509cbf6d466","name":"Vilsbøll, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-0456-6787","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip K","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Filip K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29099978"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2017-01949","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"288-294","publisher":"Endocrine Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041464998"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cff6fe60-0b54-4c4b-b70b-d53ccdcac912","sdu-4432bc9b-4213-4021-9302-f97eb103e960"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Glucose-Dependent Insulinotropic Polypeptide (GIP) Inhibits Bone Resorption Independently of Insulin and Glycemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-046357","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background Intravenous lipid emulsion (ILE) is used to treat drug poisonings. The resultant hyperlipemia may affect laboratory tests but the consequences are poorly characterized. In a clinical trial we therefore investigated the effects of ILE on laboratory tests analyzed on common analytical platforms (Roche® cobas 8000 and SYSMEX® flow-cytometry). Methods Ten healthy participants each completed 4 trial days (two with ILE and two with placebo). ILE (5.25 mL/kg) was administered from 12.5 to 30 min from baseline. At 0, 30 and 60 min, blood samples were drawn for measurement of 20 analytes. We investigated the effects of ILE on analyte levels and frequencies of exceedance of predefined analyzer hemolysis (H) or lipemia (L)-index cut-offs and test-specific reference change values (RCVs) on ILE-days. If the results were blocked due to exceedance of index values, we manually extracted the results. Results Sixteen out of 20 tests were blocked because H- or L-index cut-offs were exceeded on ILE-days. Differences in analyte levels between ILE- and placebo-days above the RCV were observed for aspartate aminotransferase, total calcium, lactate dehydrogenase (LDH), sodium and neutrophils. Mean values outside the normal range after ILE were observed for LDH (219 U/L), sodium (135.3 mmol/L) and total calcium (2.1 mmol/L). Conclusions ILE-infusion caused report failure of nearly all laboratory tests performed on a cobas 8000-platform, but it was possible to manually retrieve the results. For most test results - particularly alkaline phosphatase, bilirubin, phosphate and carbamide - the consequences of ILE were marginal, and the effects of ILE were reduced at the 60-min timepoint.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Petersen, Kasper M","Jørgensen, Niklas R","Bøgevig, Søren","Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","Jensen, Thomas B","Dalhoff, Kim","Christensen, Mikkel Bring"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047450"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Petersen, Kasper M."],"keyword":["Analytical interference","Lipemia","Reference change value","Sysmex"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of high dose intravenous lipid emulsion on laboratory tests in humans a randomized placebo controlled double blind clinical crossover trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/142932557/Effects_of_high_dose_intravenous_lipid_emulsion_on_laboratory_tests_in_humans.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-047450","identifier":[{"id":"85050166873","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30004900","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f64d5846-6f13-445d-a8f0-163504023bde","sdu-25fa46fa-7277-4ff6-88b1-2635a2819912"],"keyword":["Roche cobas","SYSMEX","analytical interference","intravenous lipid emulsion","lipemia","reference change value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9B86ED7AD406F5EF87BB3B8A83BF533D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/142932557/Effects_of_high_dose_intravenous_lipid_emulsion_on_laboratory_tests_in_humans.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper M","key":"petersenkaspermpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Kasper M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas R.","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jørgensen, Niklas R.","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"bøgevigsørenpau","last":"Bøgevig","name":"Bøgevig, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tonny S","key":"petersentonnystudsgaardpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"95e21f85-7cd9-443d-88c7-cc0b6e7bc844","name":"Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","name_org":"Petersen, Tonny S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tonny S.","key":"petersentonnyspau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Tonny S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas B","key":"jensenthomasbpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thomas B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kim P","key":"dalhoffkimpau","last":"Dalhoff","locid":"1bacc939-23ea-4041-9815-4d3b92b6d9c3","name":"Dalhoff, Kim","name_org":"Dalhoff, Kim P","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim P.","key":"dalhoffkimppau","last":"Dalhoff","name":"Dalhoff, Kim P.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mikkel B","key":"christensenmikkelbringpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"4f5c91e2-3caa-4263-8d9c-df3bfdfbd31b","name":"Christensen, Mikkel Bring","name_org":"Christensen, Mikkel B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel B.","key":"christensenmikkelbpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Mikkel B.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30004900"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/cclm-2018-0430","issn":["14346621","14374331"],"issn_org":["14346621"],"issue":"12","journal":"Clinical Chemistry and Laboratory Medicine","pages":"2047-2057","publisher":"De Gruyter","status":"p","title":"Clinical Chemistry and Laboratory Medicine","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050166873"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f64d5846-6f13-445d-a8f0-163504023bde","sdu-25fa46fa-7277-4ff6-88b1-2635a2819912"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of high-dose, intravenous lipid emulsion on laboratory tests in humans : A randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind, clinical crossover trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-047450","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Due to the localized nature of Charcot foot, systemically altered levels of inflammation markers can be difficult to measure. The aim of this study was to investigate whether it is possible to detect an arteriovenous (A-V) flux in any locally produced inflammatory biomarkers from an acute Charcot foot by comparing local and systemic measurements. Methods: We included patients with acute diabetic Charcot foot. Blood was sampled from the vena saphena magna on the distal part of the crus bilaterally as well as from the arteria radialis. To minimize the A-V shunting effect, the feet were externally cooled with ice water prior to resampling. Results: Both before and after cooling, the A-V flux of interleukin-6 (IL-6) between the Charcot feet and the arterial level was significantly higher than the flux between the healthy feet and the arterial level (Δvaluebefore: 7.25 versus 0.41 pg/mL, resp., p = 0.008; Δvalueafter: 10.04 versus 1.68 pg/mL, resp., p = 0.032). There were no differences in the fluxes for other markers of inflammation. Conclusion: We have found an increased A-V flux of IL-6 in the acute diabetic Charcot foot compared to the healthy foot in the same patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jansen, Rasmus Bo","Christensen, Tomas Møller","Bülow, Jens","Rørdam, Lene","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Svendsen, Ole Lander"],"cuid":["S02-087.15-041340"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jansen, Rasmus Bo"],"keyword":["Biomarkers blood","Case Control Studies","Female","Humans","Inflammation Mediators blood","Interleukin 6 blood","Male","Middle Aged","Up Regulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"markers of local inflammation and bone resorption in the acute diabetic charcot foot","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/5647981","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.15-041340","identifier":[{"id":"85059316933","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6098852","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30155488","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3315201c-c776-4e0d-9806-f75d60bd894d","sdu-3ab6f8fe-7ab8-4500-88fc-4bf7275507e5"],"keyword":["Arthropathy, Neurogenic/blood","Biomarkers/blood","Bone Resorption/blood","Case-Control Studies","Diabetic Foot/blood","Female","Humans","Inflammation Mediators/blood","Interleukin-6/blood","Male","Middle Aged","Up-Regulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EC9E1ADA8C5AE8C3D63D80A80343EE60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/5647981","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146231452/Markers_of_Local_Inflammation_and_Bone_Resorption_in_the_Acute_Diabetic_Charcot_Foot.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/216308087/5647981.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Rasmus Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tomas Møller","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Tomas Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bülowpau","last":"Bülow","name":"Bülow, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"rørdampau","last":"Rørdam","name":"Rørdam, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Ole Lander","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"a4602320-eec3-42f0-b4c6-450bf439b1fd","name":"Svendsen, Ole Lander","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30155488"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2018/5647981","issn":["23146745","23146753"],"issn_org":["23146745"],"journal":"Journal of Diabetes Research","paperid":"5647981","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Journal of Diabetes Research","volume":"2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059316933"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3315201c-c776-4e0d-9806-f75d60bd894d","sdu-3ab6f8fe-7ab8-4500-88fc-4bf7275507e5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Markers of Local Inflammation and Bone Resorption in the Acute Diabetic Charcot Foot","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.15-041340","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Fracture risk is increased in individuals with type 2 diabetes (T2D). The pathophysiological mechanisms accentuating fracture risk in T2D are convoluted, incorporating factors such as hyperglycaemia, insulinopenia, and antidiabetic drugs. The objectives of this study were to assess whether different insulin regimens, metformin and rosiglitazone influence bone metabolism. We explored if the concentration of metformin and rosiglitazone in blood or improved glycaemic control altered bone turnover. METHODS: Two-year clinical trial designed to investigate effects of antidiabetic treatment in 371 T2D patients. Participants were randomized to short or long-acting human insulin (non-blinded) and then further randomized to metformin + placebo, rosiglitazone + placebo, metformin + rosiglitazone or placebo + placebo (blinded). Fasting bone turnover markers (BTM) representing bone resorption (CTX) and formation (PINP) including HbA1c were measured at baseline and after 3, 12 and 24 months. Trough steady-state plasma concentrations of metformin and rosiglitazone were measured after 3, 6 and 9 months of treatment. Associations between treatments and BTMs during the follow-up of the trial were analysed in mixed-effects models that included adjustments for age, gender, BMI, renal function and repeated measures of HbA1c. RESULTS: BTMs increased from baseline to month 12 and remained higher at month 24, with CTX and PINP increasing 28.5% and 23.0% (all: p < 0.001), respectively. Allocation of insulin regimens was not associated with different levels of BTMs. Metformin and metformin + rosiglitazone but not rosiglitazone alone were associated with lower bone formation (PINP). Neither metformin nor rosiglitazone plasma concentrations was associated with BTMs. HbA1c was inversely associated with CTX but not P1NP. CONCLUSIONS: The choice of insulin treatment is not influencing BTMs, metformin treatment may decrease BTMs, and improvement of glycaemic control may influence bone resorption activity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Stage, Tore Bjerregaard","Christensen, Mette-Marie Hougaard","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Brøsen, Kim","Gram, Jeppe","Frost, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-040305"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California, San Francisco"],"keyword":["Biomarkers blood","Bone Remodeling drug effects","Bone and Bones drug effects","Bone turnover markers","Collagen Type I blood","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 blood","Female","Humans","Insulin","Insulin pharmacology","Male","Metformin","Metformin pharmacology","Middle Aged","Peptide Fragments blood","Peptides blood","Procollagen blood","Rosiglitazone","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of metformin rosiglitazone and insulin on bone metabolism in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bone.2018.04.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-040305","identifier":[{"id":"29654849","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85045380925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1252d4b6-cac7-431e-8bed-c4f8a10cc041","sdu-3da5c4e7-dc90-4bb5-a7f0-33ff75163c9d"],"keyword":["Biomarkers/blood","Bone Remodeling/drug effects","Bone and Bones/drug effects","Bone turnover markers","Collagen Type I/blood","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/blood","Female","Humans","Insulin","Insulin/pharmacology","Male","Metformin","Metformin/pharmacology","Middle Aged","Peptide Fragments/blood","Peptides/blood","Procollagen/blood","Rosiglitazone","Rosiglitazone/pharmacology","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-92460789FF48EFD148559745C26444A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bone.2018.04.004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/222320195/1_s2.0_S8756328218301509_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/140594851/Effects_of_metformin_rosiglitazone_and_insulin_on_bone_metabolism_in_patients_with_type_2_diabetes.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california san francisco","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California, San Francisco","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Biochemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine