{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: In the 1990s, the publication and PhD recruitment rates following the Danish pre-graduate research programme (PGRP) in medicine were 54% and 33%, respectively. Updated estimates are unknown. METHODS: All medical students enrolled in the PGRP at the Faculty of Medicine, Aarhus University (Health), Denmark, during 2003-2012 were included (n = 687). The PGRP files were merged with PhD students' files at Health. A systematic literature search was completed for research students who had enrolled during the 2006-2009 period (n = 227). The factors investigated were student age, sex, PGRP completion time and years in medical school at the time of PGRP initiation. Supervisors were described by sex, title, position and affiliation. Calculations were tested by the chi-squared test; p < 0.05 was considered significant. RESULTS: A larger proportion of male medical students conducted a PGRP compared to female medical students (28% versus 19%; p < 0.01). Within three and a half years from PGRP initiation, 13% of the research students had enrolled in a PhD programme at Health, and 52% had published ≥ 1 paper with ≥ 1 supervisor. The research student was the first author on 43% of the overall 224 papers, and 90% were original articles. Publication was positively associated with completion of the PGRP in < 18 months and with embarking on a PhD and with having a male main supervisor. PhD recruitment was related to enrolment in the PGRP after fewer years in medical school. CONCLUSIONS: Fast completion of the PGRP and early enrolment in the programme were associated with scientific publishing and PhD recruitment. The publication rate has remained stable over time. FUNDING: Authors were funded by their individual affiliations. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Skovgaard, Marlene","Okkels, Niels","Christensen, Mette Krogh","Telinius, Niklas","Hauge, Ellen Margrethe"],"cuid":["S02-080.69-803904"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Skovgaard, Marlene"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"publication raqte and phd enrolment following a medical pre graduate research programme","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84940370188","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.69-803904","identifier":[{"id":"26324085","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84940370188","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-096e8ba8-b67b-4ea6-93e7-e8ebd567bd83","au-3e035f8b-0f77-4f5f-87a2-357f4002570a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C81DE4885C1EDDCC769514FB6D2C856B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Affective Disorders"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marlene","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Marlene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"okkelspau","last":"Okkels","locid":"de3b80ed-a9e9-43ec-bd60-1545eadb85b2","name":"Okkels, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-6483-9505","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Krogh","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"82913481-b8b3-4c54-a3c7-ce47347ec4fe","name":"Christensen, Mette Krogh","orcid":"0000-0002-7097-9993","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niklas","key":"teliniuspau","last":"Telinius","locid":"04f890a7-8e7d-485a-9ff2-91453ec0d41c","name":"Telinius, Niklas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen-Margrethe","key":"haugepau","last":"Hauge","locid":"6e0e979f-48d6-40bd-89ec-a2502b1cefd4","name":"Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","name_org":"Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26324085"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["16039629"],"issue":"9","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","pages":"1-5","paperid":"A5134","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940370188"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-096e8ba8-b67b-4ea6-93e7-e8ebd567bd83","au-3e035f8b-0f77-4f5f-87a2-357f4002570a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Publication raqte and PhD enrolment following a medical pre-graduate research programme","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.69-803904","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Dabbling ducks (Anas spp.) are important migratory quarry species, protected as a shared resource under international legislation. However, there is a lack of sufficient high-qual- ity data on vital demographic rates and long-term trends in numbers to judge the conser- vation status of many duck populations at the flyway level. In response to reported de- clines in the North-West European flyway population of the Mallard, we compiled avail- able data on this species in the Nordic countries up to 2010. Generally, national breeding numbers showed increasing trends, wintering abundance showed variable trends, and productivity measures indicated stable or increasing trends. Major knowledge gaps were identified, namely the size of hunting bags, the influence of the released Mallards and the role of short-stopping in explaining changing patterns of wintering abundance across the North-West European flyway. Numerically the Nordic breeding population appears in “good condition”, and the wintering numbers have been either stable or increasing in the last two decades. The annual number of releases needs to be determined in order to judge the sustainability of the current levels of exploitation. Overall, none of the indicators showed alarming signs for the Mallard population in the Nordic countries when consid- ered in isolation. However, the widespread decline in wintering numbers elsewhere across North-western Europe requires urgent pan-European action.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Dalby, Lars","Söderquist, Pär","Christensen, Thomas Kjær","Clausen, Preben","Einarsson, Árni","Elmberg, Johan","Fox, Anthony David","Holmqvist, Niklas","Langendoen, Tom","Lehikoinen, Aleksi","Lindström, Åke","Lorentsen, Svein-Håkon","Nilsson, Leif","Pöysä, Hannu","Rintala, Jukka","Sigfússon, Arnór Þ.","Svenning, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-212686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Finnish Game and Fisheries Research Institute","Finnish Museum of Natural History","Kristianstad University","Lund University","Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","Wetlands International"],"keyword":["Mallard"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the status of the nordic populations of the mallard anas platyrhynchos in a changing world","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/54026900/Dalbyetal2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-212686","identifier":[{"id":"84876384978","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-92304cba-5576-4fe3-9128-4910149dc147"],"keyword":["Mallard"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-0F3FBAA6333C49E6439D0342CF1C22A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ornisfennica.org/search.htm","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/54026900/Dalbyetal2013.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Wildlife Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kristianstad university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Kristianstad University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"wetlands international","name":"Wetlands International","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fi","key":"finnish museum of natural history","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Museum of Natural History","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute for nature research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"fi","key":"finnish game and fisheries research institute","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Finnish Game and Fisheries Research Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"dalbypau","last":"Dalby","locid":"c18f2307-88c7-4519-b094-c934835e74e0","name":"Dalby, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-7270-6999","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pär","key":"söderquistpau","last":"Söderquist","name":"Söderquist, Pär","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Kjær","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"5554437a-52ef-4f5b-a1e8-7f22fbec1bee","name":"Christensen, Thomas Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Preben","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"09884c6f-eeec-4774-a4e9-db625c26dd82","name":"Clausen, Preben","orcid":"0000-0001-8986-294X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Árni","key":"einarssonpau","last":"Einarsson","name":"Ein